1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
To be continued...

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,600
I'm so sorry, Yamada. Come on, Runa, you apologize too. I'm so sorry.

3
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:39,160
I'll tie my hair up, okay?

4
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:44,140
Excuse me. I'm heading back home for a bit.

5
00:00:45,580 --> 00:00:49,000
I didn't bring over any of the tools I need, so...

6
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:50,540
Oh, but...

7
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:51,400
I'll be right back.

8
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:55,260
Wait, you don't have to do that. Isn't going back and forth a hassle?

9
00:00:55,260 --> 00:00:56,980
Don't worry. It's not far.

10
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:29,980
I'll be right back.

11
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Even if they bully me, I can deal with it.

12
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,000
As long as I have you, Akito.

13
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Let's stay together forever, even after we're all grown up.

14
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
I can't promise you that.

15
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Hi, welcome.

16
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Would you like a plastic bag for that?

17
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Yes.

18
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
This is the one you always buy.

19
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,000
It's really good, isn't it? This brand of tea?

20
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Uh, yes.

21
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
It's one of my favorites to drink, too.

22
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Thank you for your patronage.

23
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Excuse me?

24
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Uh, sorry if this is too forward, but would you mind telling me your name?

25
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,000
I've seen you in your uniform. It's Tosei Academies, right?

26
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,000
I graduated from there myself.

27
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
To be honest, I've been wanting to talk to you for a while now.

28
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,000
I'm sorry, but I'm kinda in a hurry.

29
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Right, of course you are.

30
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Why is she looking at me like that?

31
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
I mean, I am in a hurry.

32
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,000
What would I talk about with a convenience store employee?

33
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Well, this is how you always are, you know?

34
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:39,000
This isn't my thing. I don't get it.

35
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,000
I'm sure it would be better to stay away.

36
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:57,000
I'm back.

37
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,000
I'm back.

38
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,000
Is no one here?

39
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,000
They look like they're sleeping so peacefully.

40
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:28,000
I'll just be quiet while I work.

41
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Close call.

42
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,000
I'll tie my hair up, okay?

43
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,000
I'll tie my hair up, okay?

44
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,000
I'll tie my hair up, okay?

45
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:40,980
Oh, my God.

46
00:06:41,000 --> 00:07:10,980
Oh, my God.

47
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:40,980
Oh, my God.

48
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
Oh, my God.

49
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,000
What?

50
00:07:45,180 --> 00:07:46,440
Mr. Yamada!

51
00:07:48,140 --> 00:07:49,440
Why are you here?

52
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:52,240
I mean, seriously, how come?

53
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:54,240
I'm your fan.

54
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:56,080
He's familiar.

55
00:07:56,340 --> 00:07:57,440
What are you doing here?

56
00:07:58,400 --> 00:08:00,100
Well, it's complicated.

57
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:01,380
Complicated how?

58
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:03,180
I'm gonna need you to be a little more specific.

59
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:04,880
What a drag.

60
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:05,740
No way.

61
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:06,980
You're really with Akane?

62
00:08:07,300 --> 00:08:10,060
I'm on a date, and this handsome fella is my boyfriend.

63
00:08:10,180 --> 00:08:10,780
I'm not her boyfriend.

64
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:12,260
Not likely.

65
00:08:12,780 --> 00:08:17,040
After giving it some more thought, that had to have been a little charade Akane was putting on.

66
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:18,960
She always wants to look good.

67
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:24,100
And besides, trust me, I keep up with all your posts on social media every second of the day.

68
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:25,600
There's no signs of a girlfriend.

69
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:27,600
It's just business as usual, like always.

70
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:30,580
I'm definitely not misreading you, so please don't worry.

71
00:08:32,100 --> 00:08:32,940
Oh, yeah.

72
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:33,860
Almost forgot.

73
00:08:34,260 --> 00:08:37,080
The whole reason I came by today was to return something to her.

74
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:42,220
I don't see her on campus at all these days, and I don't have a way of contacting her anymore either.

75
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:46,460
These are the containers for all the lunches she's ever made me.

76
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:47,640
And her plates, too.

77
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:52,840
See, I never got around to giving them back, so now I've got a whole pile of them.

78
00:08:54,260 --> 00:08:56,420
Just counting the lunchboxes, I've got around five.

79
00:08:56,780 --> 00:08:58,740
So I figured returning them late would be better than ever.

80
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:00,300
Isn't that way too many?

81
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:04,460
Well, I'm pretty sure she doesn't want to look at me anymore.

82
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:09,300
But when I finally started clearing all this stuff, it got me thinking about her.

83
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:11,840
I made you lunch!

84
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:16,920
I didn't know if she'd been doing all right since then, and I started getting worried.

85
00:09:18,740 --> 00:09:22,260
If I saw that she was okay, I thought it would give me peace of mind.

86
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:33,240
I think she's just fine.

87
00:09:34,460 --> 00:09:37,040
Is that it?

88
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:38,700
What you came for?

89
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:45,800
To see her, and get peace of mind?

90
00:09:50,620 --> 00:09:51,460
I think...

91
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:53,580
I'll leave now.

92
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:58,080
I'm sorry, this was pretty selfish of me.

93
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:00,580
Akane doesn't need to know.

94
00:10:00,580 --> 00:10:02,120
I was never here.

95
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:08,920
You can just tell her that her old lunchboxes appeared out of the blue.

96
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:10,360
I'm counting on you, sir!

97
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:11,280
Right.

98
00:10:17,380 --> 00:10:18,780
Good luck in your next tournament!

99
00:10:18,980 --> 00:10:20,120
I'll be rooting for you!

100
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:34,740
Hey, uh...

101
00:10:34,740 --> 00:10:37,360
How much did she hear?

102
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:41,980
These lunchboxes...

103
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:43,740
Showed up out of nowhere.

104
00:10:43,740 --> 00:10:59,500
Is that so?

105
00:10:59,640 --> 00:11:01,380
That's a pretty big stretch, you know.

106
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:04,960
It's funny hearing you say that all straight-faced.

107
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:08,660
Thanks for dealing with him, though.

108
00:11:08,660 --> 00:11:15,960
Um, here.

109
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:17,220
This is yours.

110
00:11:19,360 --> 00:11:19,840
Hmm?

111
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:21,760
Oh, hey!

112
00:11:21,900 --> 00:11:23,460
It must have fallen out without me noticing!

113
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:24,380
Yes.

114
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:25,860
I took it off.

115
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:27,040
Huh?

116
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:31,500
I took it off of you, while you were sleeping.

117
00:11:32,980 --> 00:11:33,500
Oh.

118
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:36,340
Is that so?

119
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:38,940
You did that, huh?

120
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:39,480
Yeah.

121
00:11:40,060 --> 00:11:40,580
Sorry.

122
00:11:41,780 --> 00:11:42,180
What?

123
00:11:42,380 --> 00:11:42,720
Why?

124
00:11:48,940 --> 00:11:49,820
Not sure.

125
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:55,260
For some reason, I wanted to do it.

126
00:11:55,260 --> 00:11:58,600
I wonder why.

127
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:03,400
Wh-what are you talking about?

128
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:08,760
It's Eita.

129
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:12,020
Thanks for getting back to me.

130
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:14,000
Yes.

131
00:12:15,640 --> 00:12:17,860
Okay, can I tell you which parts I don't have?

132
00:12:18,260 --> 00:12:19,360
Oh, uh, hold up a sec.

133
00:12:19,720 --> 00:12:20,600
I'm gonna write it down.

134
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:22,040
Hmm, let's see.

135
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:22,180
Hmm.

136
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:27,060
What's going on?

137
00:12:27,060 --> 00:12:34,040
Miss Akane Kinoshita, right?

138
00:12:35,620 --> 00:12:37,560
Any shift preferences, or the like?

139
00:12:38,020 --> 00:12:40,960
As long as I don't have class, I can take any shift you need covered.

140
00:12:41,320 --> 00:12:41,620
Yeah?

141
00:12:41,860 --> 00:12:43,140
Well, that is good to know.

142
00:12:43,740 --> 00:12:46,360
Since your school's nearby, the commute will be easy, too, right?

143
00:12:46,760 --> 00:12:47,120
Yes.

144
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:51,700
Our store tends to get a lot of business throughout the day, so I'd like you to come in as much as possible.

145
00:12:51,860 --> 00:12:52,980
Would that be okay with you?

146
00:12:52,980 --> 00:12:53,800
Yes!

147
00:12:54,100 --> 00:12:55,120
I'll give it my all!

148
00:12:56,440 --> 00:12:58,040
Part-time at a convenience store?

149
00:12:58,220 --> 00:12:59,740
I didn't know you were applying for that.

150
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:01,420
The job's only short-term.

151
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:02,980
It's the shop near campus.

152
00:13:03,440 --> 00:13:05,860
You know, the one along the road with the long-haired manager?

153
00:13:06,580 --> 00:13:07,880
Oh, that shop, huh?

154
00:13:08,540 --> 00:13:10,000
Let me know when your ship just set.

155
00:13:10,060 --> 00:13:10,920
I'll come check you out.

156
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:12,420
Yeah, drop by.

157
00:13:13,260 --> 00:13:14,700
But why the part-time job?

158
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:17,100
Didn't they fix your broken computer for you?

159
00:13:17,100 --> 00:13:25,140
They did, but Eita, uh, my guildmate, swapped out some parts for free, and I think they'd end up being pretty expensive if I bought them myself.

160
00:13:26,260 --> 00:13:29,360
I just don't feel right about not paying for anything.

161
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:32,840
So I'm gonna ask about how much it was when I log in later.

162
00:13:33,260 --> 00:13:35,200
You're gonna ask about it in-game, huh?

163
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:35,900
Uh-huh.

164
00:13:36,660 --> 00:13:37,340
Well, yeah.

165
00:13:37,520 --> 00:13:39,300
I guess they did help you out after all.

166
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:40,860
You'll have to thank them somehow.

167
00:13:41,020 --> 00:13:41,340
Mama!

168
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:43,560
Hey, they're calling for me.

169
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:46,800
I have to get back to this group date right now, but let's chat more later.

170
00:13:47,180 --> 00:13:47,460
Okay.

171
00:13:48,460 --> 00:13:50,760
You've been in the ladies' room too long, Momo.

172
00:13:51,080 --> 00:13:52,800
The guys are waiting for you out there.

173
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:53,620
Yeah, sorry.

174
00:13:53,900 --> 00:13:55,380
I just got a call from a friend.

175
00:13:55,580 --> 00:13:56,020
A friend?

176
00:13:56,520 --> 00:13:56,960
Akane.

177
00:13:57,240 --> 00:13:58,900
It seems she got a part-time job.

178
00:13:59,260 --> 00:14:00,780
Ah, Miss Kinoshita.

179
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:03,720
Come to think of it, she never comes to our group dates anymore.

180
00:14:04,040 --> 00:14:07,540
She's been pretty busy with her online games lately, so let's leave her be.

181
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:08,820
All right!

182
00:14:09,040 --> 00:14:10,900
Today's the day I'm gonna find my prince!

183
00:14:11,340 --> 00:14:15,860
Oh, no.

184
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:20,280
Momo's ideal man sure is taking his sweet time to appear, isn't he?

185
00:14:21,860 --> 00:14:23,460
You can't give up now.

186
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:25,260
If you do, it'll be game over.

187
00:14:28,220 --> 00:14:33,860
But still, does finding your ideal man the moment you meet actually happen to people in real life?

188
00:14:39,140 --> 00:14:39,740
Hey!

189
00:14:39,740 --> 00:14:40,860
Rorihime!

190
00:14:40,860 --> 00:14:41,080
Rorihime!

191
00:14:42,580 --> 00:14:43,140
Akanechi!

192
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:45,640
Long time no see!

193
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:46,800
Hello, hello!

194
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:48,960
This is Eita, right?

195
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:52,160
What have you been up to?

196
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:53,340
Oh, not much.

197
00:14:53,500 --> 00:14:55,620
The submaster and I were having a guild meeting.

198
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:56,340
Huh?

199
00:14:56,460 --> 00:14:57,360
The submaster?

200
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:57,820
Where?

201
00:14:57,820 --> 00:14:57,860
Where?

202
00:14:57,860 --> 00:14:58,360
Where?

203
00:14:58,360 --> 00:15:01,880
Over there, see?

204
00:15:01,880 --> 00:15:02,460
Huh?

205
00:15:02,460 --> 00:15:03,820
Right there!

206
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:09,380
Oh, so small!

207
00:15:09,380 --> 00:15:13,080
The submaster is super tiny!

208
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:25,040
He's a member of the micro-nest species.

209
00:15:25,040 --> 00:15:27,500
Out of combat, they're extremely tiny.

210
00:15:28,060 --> 00:15:33,020
Sadly, they're treated as a joke amongst the community, but you can train them to become really strong.

211
00:15:33,020 --> 00:15:35,340
Ain't that right, Mr. Takuzo?

212
00:15:35,540 --> 00:15:36,740
Oh, Akane, dear.

213
00:15:36,860 --> 00:15:37,160
Hello!

214
00:15:37,820 --> 00:15:39,680
Hello, I'm Takuzo Kamata.

215
00:15:39,920 --> 00:15:43,540
My in-game character name is Takuzo as well and is spelled out in English.

216
00:15:44,260 --> 00:15:44,520
Huh?

217
00:15:44,620 --> 00:15:45,440
Mr. Kamata?

218
00:15:45,720 --> 00:15:46,640
Tsk, tsk, tsk, tsk.

219
00:15:46,820 --> 00:15:48,680
In here, we call him Mr. Takuzo.

220
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:49,820
Oh, that's right!

221
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:50,320
Sorry!

222
00:15:50,780 --> 00:15:57,360
Since Mr. Takuzo usually stays in dungeons out of farming moths, seeing him in the guild room is a rare sight, isn't it?

223
00:15:57,740 --> 00:15:58,740
He's adorable!

224
00:15:59,040 --> 00:16:01,640
But if you zoom out even a little, Mr. Takuzo disappears!

225
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:03,060
I know, right?

226
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:08,060
Oh, by the way, real quick, there's something I wanted to ask you about, Rurihime.

227
00:16:08,180 --> 00:16:09,200
Oh, what is it?

228
00:16:10,160 --> 00:16:15,180
About how much were the repair fees for the computer you fixed for me the other day.

229
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:16,440
Oh, my God!

230
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:18,040
What?

231
00:16:18,940 --> 00:16:20,180
Uh, but why?

232
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:27,860
Aw, I can't just let you do it for nothing.

233
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:28,800
What?

234
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:33,180
What do you think we should do, Mr. Takuzo?

235
00:16:33,540 --> 00:16:37,980
Well, I can certainly see where both of you are coming from, so that's a hard one.

236
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:45,220
Instead of monetary compensation, how about we compromise by asking her to take part in that plan we were discussing before she arrived?

237
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:47,640
Ha-ha! Yes, that sounds good to me!

238
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:50,580
A plan?

239
00:16:50,580 --> 00:17:06,140
Oh, MT! Here comes the Ominous Senpai!

240
00:17:06,220 --> 00:17:07,100
Huh? No way!

241
00:17:07,280 --> 00:17:08,440
Should we try talking to him?

242
00:17:08,580 --> 00:17:09,940
Huh? And say what?

243
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:12,500
Um, maybe we could bring up games?

244
00:17:12,780 --> 00:17:14,540
Ah, what was it called again?

245
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:15,580
F-P...

246
00:17:15,580 --> 00:17:17,900
Oh, someone showed up.

247
00:17:19,360 --> 00:17:19,800
Yo!

248
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:20,920
Hello.

249
00:17:21,580 --> 00:17:23,800
Trash duty? Sure looks heavy.

250
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:27,620
As usual, the girls can't take their eyes off you.

251
00:17:27,980 --> 00:17:31,460
If you just enter the pageant instead of turning it down, you'd win big time.

252
00:17:31,840 --> 00:17:34,140
I swear, your good looks are going to waste, man.

253
00:17:34,140 --> 00:17:39,060
But no matter how much you say no, the pageant committee still hasn't given up on you.

254
00:17:40,240 --> 00:17:42,360
They even asked me to talk you into it.

255
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:46,260
I feel for the girls if you ever started dating.

256
00:17:46,740 --> 00:17:48,080
They might cry a whole river.

257
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:50,520
There'd be a school-wide riot.

258
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:51,420
So?

259
00:17:52,560 --> 00:17:53,020
Ha-ha!

260
00:17:53,800 --> 00:17:54,660
Are you free today?

261
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:56,320
You want a game when we get home?

262
00:17:57,600 --> 00:17:58,040
Yamada!

263
00:17:58,800 --> 00:17:59,080
Huh?

264
00:17:59,780 --> 00:18:02,460
You left your phone in class and it's been ringing non-stop!

265
00:18:03,340 --> 00:18:04,260
Okay, thanks.

266
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:05,920
Huh?

267
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:07,820
Seriously, what was that?

268
00:18:08,300 --> 00:18:09,960
Would it kill you to be a little friendlier?

269
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:11,320
Use some charm!

270
00:18:11,740 --> 00:18:12,640
Thank you, ladies!

271
00:18:13,340 --> 00:18:16,040
Non-stop ringing must mean it's Eita, I guess.

272
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:18,400
Thank you so very much, my darling kittens!

273
00:18:18,660 --> 00:18:20,040
Or maybe you could say, uh...

274
00:18:20,040 --> 00:18:31,260
The vibration on your desk was making a lot of noise.

275
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:33,020
Too much.

276
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:34,180
Hence, the towel.

277
00:18:36,460 --> 00:18:38,160
Yeah, I'm sorry about that.

278
00:18:40,100 --> 00:18:42,220
Thank you very much, Tsubaki.

279
00:18:42,220 --> 00:18:42,320
Thank you.

280
00:18:42,320 --> 00:19:06,060
For last night's match, we were playing on an overseas server.

281
00:19:06,500 --> 00:19:07,680
So the lag was crazy...

282
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:08,880
Don't use lag as an excuse.

283
00:19:10,360 --> 00:19:10,840
Right.

284
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:31,800
Sponsor?

285
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:35,000
It's FOSS, right?

286
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:35,800
That MMO?

287
00:19:36,500 --> 00:19:37,100
Yes.

288
00:19:38,340 --> 00:19:39,220
Is it fun?

289
00:19:40,460 --> 00:19:41,060
Yes.

290
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:44,280
Uh-uh.

291
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:44,320
Uh-uh.

292
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:52,420
And it's faster now because aside from the GPU, I also upgraded the previous gen CPU and doubled your RAM.

293
00:21:52,940 --> 00:21:55,760
Oh, and I swapped out your hard drive with an SSD, too.

294
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:03,160
None of that makes sense to me. But are you saying it's like a totally different machine inside now?

295
00:22:03,500 --> 00:22:04,680
Well, basically.

296
00:22:07,820 --> 00:22:10,300
Thanks again, Yamada. I owe you one.

297
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:11,800
It's fine.

298
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:22,960
All righty then. Today we'll be having our Welcome Back Akanechi private event.

299
00:22:23,160 --> 00:22:27,840
And to celebrate the occasion, the three of us will be going on a dungeon raid tour full of daring, too.

300
00:22:28,040 --> 00:22:29,080
Let's go!

301
00:22:30,180 --> 00:22:32,480
Oh, I'm excited to go raiding with you.

302
00:22:32,940 --> 00:22:36,500
Oh, don't you worry, dear. There's no need for you to be nervous.

303
00:22:36,820 --> 00:22:41,920
At your current level, you won't have any trouble clearing today's dungeon, so you're going to be perfectly fine.

304
00:22:41,920 --> 00:22:45,700
And both of us will be right there throwing our full support behind you.

305
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:51,120
Mr. Kamata, whether it's in-game or real life, you're always so kind.

306
00:22:51,780 --> 00:22:55,700
Not to mention your avatar really suits you for some reason. So cute!

307
00:22:58,040 --> 00:23:00,200
Come on, you two! Are you ready?

308
00:23:00,800 --> 00:23:02,160
It's dungeon time!

309
00:23:02,840 --> 00:23:03,200
Yeah!

310
00:23:04,200 --> 00:23:07,840
All right. I'm going to try my best to be as useful as possible.

311
00:23:07,840 --> 00:23:35,320
– Oh, come on, play it out –

312
00:23:35,320 --> 00:23:39,500
Talk about a huge gap!

